# Without this, git's own content-sniffing heuristic decides whether a file
# is text or binary -- verified (by comparing the staged blob byte-for-byte
# against the working file) that it happened to guess right for the two
# fixture PDFs on this commit, but "happened to guess right" isn't a
# guarantee on a future checkout/recommit, especially with core.autocrlf on
# (the default on Windows, which is what generated the "LF will be replaced
# by CRLF" warning that prompted this file). Binary marks it -text -diff,
# so line-ending normalization never applies to it at all, regardless of
# what the content-sniffing heuristic would have guessed.
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
